From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:02:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Choose the base layer from /run/tiny-dfr/layer

A desktop helper writes "fn" or "media" there for the active program
(MacBookPro13,2 with a T1: F1-F12 for terminals and editors, media keys
otherwise). The file is watched with inotify; without it the configured
MediaLayerDefault stays. Holding Fn still shows the other layer.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
---
 src/config.rs       |  2 ++
 src/layer_switch.rs | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/main.rs         | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 65 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/layer_switch.rs

diff --git a/src/config.rs b/src/config.rs
index 063c318..af694ef 100644
--- a/src/config.rs
+++ b/src/config.rs
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ pub struct Config {
     pub adaptive_brightness: bool,
     pub active_brightness: u32,
     pub double_press_switch_layers: u32,
+    pub media_layer_default: bool,
 }
 
 #[derive(Deserialize)]
@@ -151,6 +152,7 @@ fn load_config(width: u16) -> (Config, [FunctionLayer; 2]) {
         font_face: load_font(&base.font_template.unwrap()),
         active_brightness: base.active_brightness.unwrap(),
         double_press_switch_layers: base.double_press_switch_layers.unwrap(),
